      "agent_input": "I'd like to review the current Q3 sales report. Could you please display it for me?",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here is the current **Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report**:\n\n---\n\n# Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim, VP of Sales | Claire Fontaine, CFO\n**Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nQ3 2026 marks another strong quarter for Meridian Analytics. Across the 15-person team, **14 deals were closed** out of 22 opportunities, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The sales pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals in the pending stage. Customer support ticket volume held steady, with critical issues resolved same-day in all cases.\n\n---\n\n## Sales Performance\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Total Closed Revenue** | $1,040,000 |\n| **Top Region** | South \u2014 $468,000 in won deals |\n| **Win Rate** | 63.6% (above the 55% company target) |\n| **Active Opportunities** | 22 |\n| **Deals Won** | 14 |\n| **Pending Deals** | ~$240,000 (expected to close by end of September) |\n\nThe three-person field sales team \u2014 **James Okafor**, **Sofia Delgado**, and **Marcus Webb** \u2014 collectively worked 22 active opportunities. Product mix shifted toward **Meridian Insights Pro**, which accounted for the majority of closed revenue. **Meridian DataBridge** continues as a strong land-and-expand vehicle with upsell opportunities maturing in Q4.\n\n---\n\n## Key Highlights\n\n- \ud83c\udfc6 **Top Deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract with a Southern-region enterprise customer on Sept 5 (D019).\n- \ud83d\udc65 **Team Headcount:** 15 employees across 5 departments \u2014 Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), Finance (2).\n- \u2705 **Support SLA:** All critical-priority tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) resolved within 24 hours.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **License Utilisation:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) at **94% capacity** \u2014 procurement review scheduled for October.\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Close the pending deals (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end.\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target **$1.2M** in new ARR.\n3. Resolve open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of quarterly customer success calls.\n4. Conduct license capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October.\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi to support Q4 roadmap.\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to dive deeper into any section \u2014 for example, a breakdown by sales rep, a monthly trend analysis, or details on the pending deals?",
        "status_code": null
      },
